    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1056">

                <pb facs="1348" n="1338" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1338"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.8571/6–346</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in China </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-06-06T18:00:00-04:00">June 6, 1946—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>247. Satisfactory await reply Chinese Govt to representations already made on
                    exemption agencies and officials US Govt from taxes. Urtel 908 June 3. Keep Dept
                        informed.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d1056-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai as Deptel 1003.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1056-f1" n="9" xml:id="d1056-f1-content">
                <p>A reply from the Chinese Foreign Office, dated August 10, referred only to the
                    income tax on lease of property and said exemption could not be granted as tax
                    was on the lessor of the property (Nanking Embassy file 851.2 Shanghai house
                    tax).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
